{"adjusted_val_bpb": 0.45803386366971904, "attempt": 0, "charged": true, "critic": {"issues": ["No measurement circumvention found: no file or network access, no pasted predictions, no use of test labels. Test SMILES are only featurized (Gobbi pharmacophore bits, physchem descriptors), and all fitted statistics (pmu/psd, Ridge coefficients, residual mu/sd) are derived from training rows only.", "No result-invalidating bug. Ridge is fit on rank-transformed training y; SVR is fit on standardized residuals and the inverse transform (pred*sd + mu + r_test) is applied consistently. Spearman is invariant to the monotone rank transform of the target.", "Minor: residuals come from in-sample Ridge predictions, so the SVR sees slightly optimistic residuals. With alpha=10 on 7 features this leak is internal to the training fold and negligible, not a validity problem.", "Minor: Gobbi bits are folded via b % 4096, which introduces collisions; harmless but arbitrary. Also Descriptors is used without a new import, so it must already be imported in the incumbent (the job ran, so it is).", "Evidence is thin: one candidate run vs one incumbent run. A replicate would be worth a slot before treating the ~0.025 gain as settled.", "No claims in the diff that conflict with the reported numbers."], "ok": true, "veto": false}, "decision": "accept", "description": "Adds a Gobbi 2D pharmacophore Tanimoto kernel (hashed to 4096 bins) averaged equally with the Morgan-Tanimoto and descriptor-RBF kernels, and fits the SVR on the residual of a Ridge(alpha=10) model on seven standardized physchem descriptors fit to the rank-normalized target.", "edit_class": "structural", "flags": [], "gpu": "willow", "idea_id": "b013", "incumbent_after": {"mean": 0.48298894804715264, "n": 1}, "incumbent_before": {"mean": 0.48298894804715264, "n": 1}, "job_id": "B1F_clear_HH_1_s0-candidate-7_1795055048569", "kind": "candidate", "lint": {"hard": [], "ok": true, "warnings": []}, "model_calls": [{"cost_usd_nominal": 0